      {"@type":"Question","name":"Can you migrate from Bubble / Webflow / FlutterFlow without rewriting from scratch?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Partially. The DATA migrates cleanly — we extract your Bubble database schema, transform it into PostgreSQL, and re-import. The UI is usually a clean rewrite (no-code visual output doesn't translate to maintainable React/Next.js) but we can match your existing design pixel-perfect. The BUSINESS LOGIC is usually faster to rewrite than to reverse-engineer from Bubble's workflow graphs. Total migration: 6-14 weeks depending on complexity."}},
      {"@type":"Question","name":"What does Bubble actually cost at scale?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Bubble's pricing is workload-unit based. A typical pre-PMF startup: $29-$99/mo. A 2K-user marketplace or B2B SaaS: $349-$649/mo. A 20K-user app with heavy workflows: $1000+/mo + workload overages. Webflow CMS sites top out around $235/mo. FlutterFlow is $50-$70/mo per developer + native compile costs. None of these include the human cost of Bubble-specialist developers (≈$80-$150/hr) which rivals custom dev rates."}},
      {"@type":"Question","name":"Is no-code 'real' technology buyers should consider?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Absolutely. We recommend Bubble, Webflow and FlutterFlow to ~30% of founders we talk to. For pre-PMF validation, internal tools, B2C landing-page-driven funnels, and simple two-sided marketplaces, no-code is genuinely faster and cheaper than custom. The trap is using no-code past its sweet spot — at which point custom catches up on cost and beats it on every other dimension."}},
      {"@type":"Question","name":"What about hybrid — keep Webflow front-end, custom backend?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, this is increasingly common. Webflow remains best-in-class for marketing-site + blog + landing pages (you keep marketing-team ownership). Custom backend + custom web app handle the authenticated product. We've built this pattern 25+ times — fastest of both worlds, low cognitive overhead. The seam is API-driven auth + payments + analytics."}},
      {"@type":"Question","name":"What if I'm not technical and I'm scared of custom?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Reasonable fear. The mitigations: (1) fixed-quote contracts so you know the all-in cost before signing; (2) weekly demos with screen-share — you see progress visually, not in tickets; (3) 100% source-code ownership in your private GitHub from day 1; (4) named senior owner you can call/text directly; (5) AMC retainer so you're not abandoned post-launch. Many of our buyers are non-technical founders. Most stick with us 22+ months."}}
